      "writtenOn": "2021-10-28T08:30:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree that it\u0027s misnamed; it\u0027s documented to mean \"requires a physical device\", with the doc saying \"It will be executed only if the test is running on the physical android device\":\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/androidx/test/filters/RequiresDevice\n\nI think this is the canonical annotation to use to mean \"don\u0027t run on virtual devices\".\n\nIt\u0027s true that the tests could run on virtual devices if they had better networking support. I think we\u0027ll have to re-enable them when that\u0027s the case, but until now we\u0027ve had to disable them so the rest of the tests can pass on such devices (particularly in presubmit).",
